Hi,

the best way to read and write labels is using rk.get.label() and rk.set.label().
The internal format for storing the meta-information might change in the future,
but these functions will likely remain unchanged. However, rk.set.label() was
not added until version 0.4.5.

Viewing labels is broken in rkward 0.4.8, indeed. Thanks for pointing this out.
This is now fixed in the current development sources (see
http://rkward.sourceforge.net/wiki/index.php?title=RKWard_SVN, if you would
like to give it a try). Alternatively, you could use version 0.4.7a for now,
which does not have this particular bug.

You write that 0.4.8 is very slow on your system. Is this for all operations,
or only for some? Could you perhaps provide some example code?

Thanks!
Thomas

